All agree to within quadrature error. Note the e case: I(e) = 0 exactly, since ln(e·x)/e³ is antisymmetric under x → e/x... equivalently the integrand's log-mean cancels — a good consistency check that the (ln a − 1) coefficient is right, not just (ln a).

So for all a > 0:

I(a) = (π/(4a³))(ln a − 1)